        "title": "test(shared): add unit tests for gateway method policy helpers",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Problem: `resolveReservedGatewayMethodScope` and `normalizePluginGatewayMethodScope` are exported pure functions enforcing operator admin scope with 0% test coverage.\n- Root cause: No test file existed.\n- Fix: Add 10 unit tests covering reserved method prefixes (exec.approvals, config, wizard, update), non-reserved methods, scope coercion, and undefined handling.\n- Out of scope: No source changes; test-only addition.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: Reserved gateway methods return `operator.admin` scope; non-reserved return undefined.\n- Real environment tested: Node.js v22, production functions from `src/shared/gateway-method-policy.js`\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch: imported via `node --import tsx -e`\n- Evidence after fix:\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx -e \"import { resolveReservedGatewayMethodScope } from ./src/shared/gateway-method-policy.js\"\n\nresolveReservedGatewayMethodScope(\"exec.approvals.list\") → \"operator.admin\"\nresolveReservedGatewayMethodScope(\"config.get\")          → \"operator.admin\"\nresolveReservedGatewayMethodScope(\"tasks.list\")          → undefined\n\n$ npx vitest run src/shared/gateway-method-policy.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  10 passed (10)\n```\n\n- Observed result after fix: All 10 tests pass; scope classification is correct.\n- What was not tested: Gateway RPC handler integration with the scope enforcement middleware.",
